  "evidence": "TEXT_F: Specific pledges on top domestic concerns—NHS Patient’s Guarantee with maximum waits and treatment choice; GP/hospital choice and more high‑throughput surgery; “Free Schools,” more per‑pupil funding, easier exclusions, and parental triggers; more police and action on antisocial behaviour; £8bn tax cuts including 6p off fuel duty and higher pensioner allowances; transport focus on roads/rail and lorry charging; pensions and elderly support. TEXT_C: Core commitment to leave the EU (repeal ECA, keep the pound) and claim an “Independence Dividend”; secondary domestic proposals (decentralise NHS, raise nurse pay; more teachers; more police; fuel duty −9p) framed within EU‑exit savings and deregulation.",
